{
  "title": "Incident of Abd al-Rahman ibn Sayyabah and the Advice of Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.)",
  "data": "'Abd al-Rahman ibn Sayyabah reports: When my father died, one of his friends came to us and knocked at the door. When I opened it, he expressed his sympathy to me and asked whether my father had left us any inheritance. When I said no, the man handed me a bag of one thousand dirhams and advised me to look after them, trade with them, and live off their profits. Rejoicing at this, I hurried to my mother and told her what had happened.\nLater, I went to another of my father's friends and asked him what kind of business I should do with the money. He advised me to trade in a fine kind of cloth, bought a quantity of it for me, and I took a shop to work in. Almighty Allah gave me a great deal of profit in this business.\nIn the season of the hajj, I intended to go on pilgrimage and told my mother so. She advised me to give the money back to its owner. When I did, the man was as happy as if I had given him the money as a gift. He offered me more money, but I thanked him and told him that I was going on the hajj. I then left for Makkah, and afterwards went on to Madinah.\nWith a group of people, I went to visit Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.), who at that time used to let all people visit him. Being young, I sat in the last row. People asked the Imam (a.s.) their questions, he answered them all, and they left. When only a few people remained, the Imam (a.s.) beckoned me to come close to him and asked, “Do you need anything?”\n“May Allah accept me as your ransom! I am 'Abd al-Rahman, the son of Sayyabah,” I answered. The Imam (a.s.) asked about my father, and I told him that he had died. Expressing his sympathy, the Imam (a.s.) asked, “Did he leave you any inheritance?” “No, he did not,” I answered. “Then how could you afford this journey of hajj?” asked the Imam (a.s.). I told him the story of the dirhams. Interrupting me, the Imam (a.s.) asked, “What did you do with the dirhams before you came on hajj?” I answered that I had given them back to their owner. “Well done,” said the Imam (a.s.). “May I give you some advice?” “Yes,” I answered. He said, “If you hold fast to telling the truth and returning what is entrusted to you, you will share in the wealth of all people.”\nThat is, the Imam (a.s.) advised him always to tell the truth and never to lie, to keep his promises, to repay his debts on time, and never to consume other people's dues wrongfully. When someone deals with people in this way, they will give him whatever he asks, and it is as if he has a share in their wealth.\n'Abd al-Rahman added: As I held to this advice of Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.), I made so much profit that in one year the religious tax due on it was three hundred thousand dirhams.\nIbn Mahbub is reported to have said: Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) taught a man this supplicatory prayer to say in his supplications:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّىْۤ اَسْئَلُكَ بِرَحْمَتِكَ الَّتِىْ لَا تُنَالُ مِنْكَ اِلَّا بِرِضَاكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS'ALUKA BIRAHMATIKAL LATEE LAA TUNAALU MINKA ILLAA BIRIDAAK\nO Allah, I ask You by Your mercy, which is not obtained from You except through Your good pleasure,\nوَالْخُرُوْجَ مِنْ جَمِيْعِ مَعَاصِيْكَ وَالدُّخُوْلَ فِىْ كُلِّ مَا يُرْضِيْكَ\nWAL KHUROOJA MIN JAMEE'I MA'AASEEKA WAD DUKHOOLA FEE KULLI MAA YURDEEK\n(and I ask You for) departure from all acts of disobedience to You, entry into all that pleases You,\nوَالنَّجَاةَ مِنْ كُلِّ وَرْطَةٍ وَالْمَخْرَجَ مِنْ كُلِّ كَبِيْرَةٍ\nWAN NAJAATA MIN KULLI WARTATIN WAL MAKHRAJA MIN KULLI KABEERAH\nsalvation from every predicament, and a way out of every grave sin\nاَتٰى بِهَا مِنِّىْ عَمْدٌ اَوْ زَلَّ بِهَا مِنِّىْ خَطَاٌ اَوْ خَطَرَ بِهَا عَلَىَّ خَطَرَاتُ الشَّيْطَانِ\nATAA BIHAA MINNEE A'MDUN AW ZALLA BIHAA MINNEE KHATA'UN AW KHATARA BIHAA A'LAYYA KHATARAATUSH SHAYTAAN\nthat I committed deliberately, or into which I slipped by mistake, or which the promptings of Satan brought to my mind.\nاَسْئَلُكَ خَوْفًا تُوْقِفُنِىْ بِهٖ عَلٰى حُدُوْدِ رِضَاكَ\nAS'ALUKA KHAWFAN TOOQIFUNEE BIHEE A'LAA HUDOODI RIDAAK\nI ask You for a fear by which You keep me within the bounds of Your good pleasure,\nوَتَشَعَّبَ بِهٖ عَنِّىْ كُلُّ شَهْوَةٍ خَطَرَ بِهَا هَوَاىَ وَاسْتُزِلَّ بِهَا رَاْيِىْ لِيُجَاوِزَ حَدَّ حَلَالِكَ\nWA TASHA'ABA BIHEE A'NNEE KULLU SHAHWATIN KHATARA BIHAA HAWAAYA WASTUZILLA BIHAA RA'YEE LIYUJAAWIZA HADDA HALAALIK\nand by which every desire is driven away from me that my passion has prompted and by which my judgment has been made to slip, so as to overstep the limit of what You have made lawful.\nاَسْئَلُكَ اَللّٰهُمَّ الْاَخْذَ بِاَحْسَنِ مَا تَعْلَمُ وَتَرْكَ سَيِّئِ كُلِّ مَا تَعْلَمُ\nAS'ALUKA ALLAAHUMMAL AKHDHA BI-AHSANI MAA TA'LAMU WA TARKA SAYYI'I KULLI MAA TA'LAM\nI ask You, O Allah, (that I) hold to the best of what You know and abandon the evil of all that You know,\nاَوْ اُخْطِئُ مِنْ حَيْثُ لَا اَعْلَمُ اَوْ مِنْ حَيْثُ اَعْلَمُ\nAW UKHTI'U MIN HAYTHU LAA A'LAMU AW MIN HAYTHU A'LAM\nor wherein I err, unknowingly or knowingly.\nاَسْئَلُكَ السَّعَةَ فِى الرِّزْقِ وَالزُّهْدَ فِى الْكَفَافِ\nAS'ALUKAS SA'ATA FIR RIZQI WAZ ZUHDA FIL KAFAAF\nI ask You for abundance in sustenance and contentment with what is sufficient,\nوَالْمَخْرَجَ بِالْبَيَانِ مِنْ كُلِّ شُبْهَةٍ وَالصَّوَابَ فِىْ كُلِّ حُجَّةٍ وَالصِّدْقَ فِىْ جَمِيْعِ الْمَوَاطِنِ\nWAL MAKHRAJA BIL BAYAANI MIN KULLI SHUBHATIN WAS SAWAABA FEE KULLI HUJJATIN WAS SIDQA FEE JAMEE'IL MAWAATIN\na way out of every doubtful matter through clear proof, rightness in every argument, and truthfulness in all situations,\nوَاِنْصَافَ النَّاسِ مِنْ نَفْسِىْ فِيْمَا عَلَىَّ وَلِىَ\nWA INSAAFAN NAASI MIN NAFSEE FEEMAA A'LAYYA WA LEE\nfairness from myself to people in what is due from me and what is due to me,\nوَالتَّذَلُّلَ فِىْ اِعْطَاۤءِ النَّصَفِ مِنْ جَمِيْعِ مَوَاطِنِ السَّخَطِ وَالرِّضَا\nWAT TADHALLULA FEE I'TAA'IN NASAFI MIN JAMEE'I MAWAATINIS SAKHATI WAR RIDAA\nhumility in giving what is fair in all situations, of anger and of pleasure alike,\nوَتَرْكَ قَلِيْلِ الْبَغْىِ وَكَثِيْرِهٖ فِى الْقَوْلِ مِنِّىْ وَالْفِعْلِ\nWA TARKA QALEELIL BAGHYI WA KATHEERIHEE FIL QAWLI MINNEE WAL FI'L\nthe abandonment of transgression, little and much, in my words and my deeds,\nوَتَمَامَ نِعَمِكَ فِىْ جَمِيْعِ الْاَشْيَاۤءِ وَالشُّكْرَ لَكَ عَلَيْهَا لِكَىْ تَرْضٰى وَبَعْدَ الرِّضَا\nWA TAMAAMA NI'AMIKA FEE JAMEE'IL ASHYAA'I WASH SHUKRA LAKA A'LAYHAA LIKAY TARDAA WA BA'DAR RIDAA\nthe completion of Your blessings in all things, and thanks to You for them, so that You may be pleased, and after You are pleased.\nوَاَسْئَلُكَ الْخِيَرَةَ فِىْ كُلِّ مَا يَكُوْنُ فِيْهِ الْخِيَرَةُ بِمَيْسُوْرِ الْاُمُوْرِ كُلِّهَا لَا بِمَعْسُوْرِهَا\nWA AS'ALUKAL KHIYARATA FEE KULLI MAA YAKOONU FEEHIL KHIYARATU BIMAYSOORIL UMOORI KULLIHAA LAA BIMA'SOORIHAA\nAnd I ask You for what is best in everything in which there is a better choice, by way of the easy course of all affairs, not the difficult one.\nيَا كَرِيْمُ يَا كَرِيْمُ يَا كَرِيْمُ وَافْتَحْ لِىْ بَابَ الْاَمْرِ الَّذِىْ فِيْهِ الْعَافِيَةُ وَالْفَرَجُ\nYAA KAREEMU YAA KAREEMU YAA KAREEMU WAFTAH LEE BAABAL AMRIL LADHEE FEEHIL A'AFIYATU WAL FARAJ\nO Generous! O Generous! O Generous! Open for me the door of the affair in which there are well-being and relief;\nوَافْتَحْ لِىْ بَابَهٗ وَيَسِّرْ لِىْ مَخْرَجَهٗ\nWAFTAH LEE BAABAHOO WA YASSIR LEE MAKHRAJAH\nopen its door for me, and make its way out easy for me.\nوَمَنْ قَدَّرْتَ لَهٗ عَلَىَّ مَقْدُوْرَةً مِنْ خَلْقِكَ فَخُذْ عَنِّىْ بِسَمْعِهٖ وَبَصَرِهٖ وَلِسَانِهٖ وَيَدِهٖ\nWA MAN QADDARTA LAHOO A'LAYYA MAQDOORATAN MIN KHALQIKA FAKHUDH A'NNEE BISAM'IHEE WA BASARIHEE WA LISAANIHEE WA YADIH\nAnd whoever of Your creatures You have given power over me, seize from me his hearing, his sight, his tongue and his hand;\nوَخُذْهُ عَنْ يَمِيْنِهٖ وَعَنْ يَسَارِهٖ وَمِنْ خَلْفِهٖ وَمِنْ قُدَّامِهٖ وَامْنَعْهُ اَنْ يَصِلَ اِلَىَّ بِسُوْۤءٍ\nWA KHUDH-HU A'N YAMEENIHEE WA A'N YASAARIHEE WA MIN KHALFIHEE WA MIN QUDDAAMIHEE WAMNA'HU AN YASILA ILAYYA BISOO'\nseize him from his right and from his left, from behind him and from in front of him, and prevent him from reaching me with harm.\nعَزَّ جَارُكَ وَجَلَّ ثَنَاۤءُ وَجْهِكَ وَلَاۤ اِلٰهَ غَيْرُكَ اَنْتَ رَبِّىْ وَاَنَا عَبْدُكَ\nA'ZZA JAARUKA WA JALLA THANAA'U WAJHIKA WA LAA ILAAHA GHAYRUKA ANTA RABBEE WA ANAA A'BDUK\nMighty is he whom You protect, and majestic is the praise of Your Face; there is no god other than You. You are my Lord, and I am Your servant.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اَنْتَ رَجَاۤئِىْ فِىْ كُلِّ كُرْبَةٍ وَاَنْتَ ثِقَتِىْ فِىْ كُلِّ شِدَّةٍ\nALLAAHUMMA ANTA RAJAA'EE FEE KULLI KURBATIN WA ANTA THIQATEE FEE KULLI SHIDDAH\nO Allah, You are my hope in every distress, and You are my trust in every hardship,\nوَاَنْتَ لِىْ فِىْ كُلِّ اَمْرٍ نَزَلَ بِىْ ثِقَةٌ وَعُدَّةٌ\nWA ANTA LEE FEE KULLI AMRIN NAZALA BEE THIQATUN WA U'DDAH\nand in every matter that befalls me, You are my trust and my provision.\nفَكَمْ مِنْ كَرْبٍ يَضْعُفُ عَنْهُ الْفُؤَادُ وَتَقِلُّ فِيْهِ الْحِيْلَةُ وَيَشْمَتُ بِهِ الْعَدُوُّ وَتَعْيٰى فِيْهِ الْاُمُوْرُ\nFAKAM MIN KARBIN YAD'UFU A'NHUL FU'AADU WA TAQILLU FEEHIL HEELATU WA YASHMATU BIHIL A'DUWWU WA TA'YAA FEEHIL UMOOR\nHow many a distress, in which the heart grows weak and means grow few, over which the enemy gloats and in which affairs become intractable,\nاَنْزَلْتُهٗ بِكَ وَشَكَوْتُهٗ اِلَيْكَ رَاغِبًا اِلَيْكَ فِيْهِ عَمَّنْ سِوَاكَ قَدْ فَرَّجْتَهٗ وَكَفَيْتَهٗ\nANZALTUHOO BIKA WA SHAKAWTUHOO ILAYKA RAAGHIBAN ILAYKA FEEHI A'MMAN SIWAAKA QAD FARRAJTAHOO WA KAFAYTAH\nhave I brought before You and complained of to You, turning to You in it rather than to anyone else, and You have relieved it and sufficed me against it!\nفَاَنْتَ وَلِىُّ كُلِّ نِعْمَةٍ وَصَاحِبُ كُلِّ حَاجَةٍ وَمُنْتَهٰى كُلِّ رَغْبَةٍ فَلَكَ الْحَمْدُ كَثِيْرًا وَلَكَ الْمَنُّ فَاضِلًا\nFA-ANTA WALIYYU KULLI NI'MATIN WA SAAHIBU KULLI HAAJATIN WA MUNTAHAA KULLI RAGHBATIN FALAKAL HAMDU KATHEERAN WA LAKAL MANNU FAADILAA\nSo You are the Master of every blessing, the Fulfiller of every need, and the Final End of every desire. To You belongs abundant praise, and to You belongs surpassing favor.\nThrough a considerable chain of narrators, Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a.s.) is reported to have taught this supplicatory prayer to Abu Basir to say in his supplications:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّىْۤ اَسْئَلُكَ قَوْلَ التَّوَّابِيْنَ وَعَمَلَهُمْ وَنُوْرَ الْاَنْبِيَاۤءِ وَصِدْقَهُمْ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS'ALUKA QAWLAT TAWWAABEENA WA A'MALAHUM WA NOORAL ANBIYAA'I WA SIDQAHUM\nO Allah, I ask You for the speech of the penitent and their deeds, the light of the prophets and their truthfulness,\nوَنَجَاةَ الْمُجَاهِدِيْنَ وَثَوَابَهُمْ وَشُكْرَ الْمُصْطَفَيْنَ وَنَصِيْحَتَهُمْ\nWA NAJAATAL MUJAAHIDEENA WA THAWAABAHUM WA SHUKRAL MUSTAFAYNA WA NASEEHATAHUM\nthe salvation of those who strive (in Your way) and their reward, the gratitude of the chosen ones and their sincerity,\nوَعَمَلَ الذَّاكِرِيْنَ وَيَقِيْنَهُمْ وَاِيْمَانَ الْعُلَمَاۤءِ وَفِقْهَهُمْ وَتَعَبُّدَ الْخَاشِعِيْنَ وَتَوَاضُعَهُمْ\nWA A'MALADH DHAAKIREENA WA YAQEENAHUM WA EEMAANAL U'LAMAA'I WA FIQHAHUM WA TA'ABBUDAL KHAASHI'EENA WA TAWAADU'AHUM\nthe deeds of those who remember (You) and their certainty, the faith of the learned and their understanding, the devotion of the humble and their modesty,\nوَحُكْمَ الْفُقَهَاۤءِ وَسِيْرَتَهُمْ وَخَشْيَةَ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ وَرَغْبَتَهُمْ\nWA HUKMAL FUQAHAA'I WA SEERATAHUM WA KHASHYATAL MUTTAQEENA WA RAGHBATAHUM\nthe wisdom of the jurists and their conduct, the awe of the God-fearing and their longing,\nوَتَصْدِيْقَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَتَوَكُّلَهُمْ وَرَجَاۤءَ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ وَبِرَّهُمْ\nWA TASDEEQAL MU'MINEENA WA TAWAKKULAHUM WA RAJAA'AL MUHSINEENA WA BIRRAHUM\nthe belief of the faithful and their reliance (on You), and the hope of those who do good and their righteousness.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّىْۤ اَسْئَلُكَ ثَوَابَ الشَّاكِرِيْنَ وَمَنْزِلَةَ الْمُقَرَّبِيْنَ وَمُرَافَقَةَ النَّبِيِّيْنَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS'ALUKA THAWAABASH SHAAKIREENA WA MANZILATAL MUQARRABEENA WA MURAAFAQATAN NABIYYEEN\nO Allah, I ask You for the reward of the grateful, the rank of those brought near (to You), and the company of the prophets.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّىْۤ اَسْئَلُكَ خَوْفَ الْعَامِلِيْنَ لَكَ وَعَمَلَ الْخَاۤئِفِيْنَ مِنْكَ وَخُشُوْعَ الْعَابِدِيْنَ لَكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS'ALUKA KHAWFAL A'AMILEENA LAKA WA A'MALAL KHAA'IFEENA MINKA WA KHUSHOO'AL A'ABIDEENA LAK\nO Allah, I ask You for the fear of those who work for You, the work of those who fear You, the humility of those who worship You,\nوَيَقِيْنَ الْمُتَوَكِّلِيْنَ عَلَيْكَ وَتَوَكُّلَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ بِكَ\nWA YAQEENAL MUTAWAKKILEENA A'LAYKA WA TAWAKKULAL MU'MINEENA BIK\nthe certainty of those who rely on You, and the reliance of those who believe in You.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّكَ بِحَاجَتِىْ عَالِمٌ غَيْرُ مُعَلَّمٍ وَاَنْتَ لَهَا وَاسِعٌ غَيْرُ مُتَكَلِّفٍ\nALLAAHUMMA INNAKA BIHAAJATEE A'ALIMUN GHAYRU MU'ALLAMIN WA ANTA LAHAA WAASI'UN GHAYRU MUTAKALLIF\nO Allah, You know my need without being taught, and You are able to meet it without effort.\nوَاَنْتَ الَّذِىْ لَا يُحْفِيْكَ سَاۤئِلٌ وَلَا يَنْقُصُكَ نَاۤئِلٌ وَلَا يَبْلُغُ مِدْحَتَكَ قَوْلُ قَاۤئِلٍ\nWA ANTAL LADHEE LAA YUHFEEKA SAA'ILUN WA LAA YANQUSUKA NAA'ILUN WA LAA YABLUGHU MID-HATAKA QAWLU QAA'IL\nYou are He Whom no asker wearies, Whom no gift diminishes, and Whose praise no speaker's words can reach.\nاَنْتَ كَمَا تَقُوْلُ وَفَوْقَ مَا نَقُوْلُ\nANTA KAMAA TAQOOLU WA FAWQA MAA NAQOOL\nYou are as You say, and above what we say.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْ لِىْ فَرَجًا قَرِيْبًا وَاَجْرًا عَظِيْمًا وَسَتْرًا جَمِيْلًا\nALLAAHUMMAJ A'L LEE FARAJAN QAREEBAN WA AJRAN A'ZEEMAN WA SATRAN JAMEELAA\nO Allah, grant me a near relief, a great reward and a beautiful covering.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّكَ تَعْلَمُ اَنِّىْ عَلٰى ظُلْمِىْ لِنَفْسِىْ وَاِسْرَافِىْ عَلَيْهَا\nALLAAHUMMA INNAKA TA'LAMU ANNEE A'LAA ZULMEE LINAFSEE WA ISRAAFEE A'LAYHAA\nO Allah, You know that, despite my wronging myself and my excesses against it,\nلَمْ اَتَّخِذْ لَكَ ضِدًّا وَلَا نِدًّا وَلَا صَاحِبَةً وَلَا وَلَدًا\nLAM ATTAKHIDH LAKA DIDDAN WA LAA NIDDAN WA LAA SAAHIBATAN WA LAA WALADAA\nI have not taken for You any opponent, nor equal, nor consort, nor son.\nيَا مَنْ لَا تُغَلِّطُهُ الْمَسَاۤئِلُ وَيَا مَنْ لَا يَشْغَلُهٗ شَيْءٌ عَنْ شَيْءٍ وَلَا سَمْعٌ عَنْ سَمْعٍ وَلَا بَصَرٌ عَنْ بَصَرٍ\nYAA MAN LAA TUGHALLITUHUL MASAA'ILU WA YAA MAN LAA YASHGHALUHOO SHAY'UN A'N SHAY'IN WA LAA SAM'UN A'N SAM'IN WA LAA BASARUN A'N BASAR\nO He Whom requests do not confuse! O He Whom nothing distracts from anything else, nor any hearing from another hearing, nor any seeing from another seeing,\nوَلَا يُبْرِمُهٗ اِلْحَاحُ الْمُلِحِّيْنَ\nWA LAA YUBRIMUHOO ILHAAHUL MULIHHEEN\nand Whom the insistence of the insistent does not weary!\nاَسْئَلُكَ اَنْ تُفَرِّجَ عَنِّىْ فِىْ سَاعَتِىْ هٰذِهٖ مِنْ حَيْثُ اَحْتَسِبُ وَمِنْ حَيْثُ لَاۤ اَحْتَسِبُ\nAS'ALUKA AN TUFARRIJA A'NNEE FEE SAA'ATEE HAADHIHEE MIN HAYTHU AHTASIBU WA MIN HAYTHU LAA AHTASIB\nI ask You to relieve me at this very hour, from where I expect and from where I do not expect;\nاِنَّكَ تُحْيِى الْعِظَامَ وَهِىَ رَمِيْمٌ اِنَّكَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ\nINNAKA TUHYIL I'ZAAMA WA HIYA RAMEEMUN INNAKA A'LAA KULLI SHAY'IN QADEER\nsurely You give life to the bones when they are decayed; surely You have power over all things.\nيَا مَنْ قَلَّ شُكْرِىْ لَهٗ فَلَمْ يَحْرِمْنِىْ وَعَظُمَتْ خَطِيْۤئَتِىْ فَلَمْ يَفْضَحْنِىْ وَرَاٰنِىْ عَلَى الْمَعَاصِىْ فَلَمْ يَجْبَهْنِىْ\nYAA MAN QALLA SHUKREE LAHOO FALAM YAHRIMNEE WA A'ZUMAT KHATEE'ATEE FALAM YAFDAHNEE WA RA'AANEE A'LAL MA'AASEE FALAM YAJBAHNEE\nO He for Whom my thanks were little, yet He did not deprive me; my sins were great, yet He did not disgrace me; He saw me committing acts of disobedience, yet He did not rebuff me;\nوَخَلَقَنِىْ لِلَّذِىْ خَلَقَنِىْ لَهٗ فَصَنَعْتُ غَيْرَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَنِىْ لَهٗ\nWA KHALAQANEE LILLADHEE KHALAQANEE LAHOO FASANA'TU GHAYRAL LADHEE KHALAQANEE LAH\nHe created me for that for which He created me, yet I did other than that for which He created me.\nفَنِعْمَ الْمَوْلٰى اَنْتَ يَا سَيِّدِىْ وَبِئْسَ الْعَبْدُ اَنَا وَجَدْتَنِىْ\nFANI'MAL MAWLAA ANTA YAA SAYYIDEE WA BI'SAL A'BDU ANAA WAJADTANEE\nHow excellent a Master You are, O my Master, and how wretched a servant You have found me!\nوَنِعْمَ الطَّالِبُ اَنْتَ رَبِّىْ وَبِئْسَ الْمَطْلُوْبُ اَلْفَيْتَنِىْ\nWA NI'MAT TAALIBU ANTA RABBEE WA BI'SAL MATLOOBU ALFAYTANEE\nHow excellent a Seeker You are, my Lord, and how wretched a one sought You have found me!\nعَبْدُكَ ابْنُ عَبْدِكَ ابْنُ اَمَتِكَ بَيْنَ يَدَيْكَ مَا شِئْتَ صَنَعْتَ بِىْ\nA'BDUKABNU A'BDIKABNU AMATIKA BAYNA YADAYKA MAA SHI'TA SANA'TA BEE\nHere before You is Your servant, the son of Your servant, the son of Your bondwoman; do with me whatever You will.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ هَدَاَتِ الْاَصْوَاتُ وَسَكَنَتِ الْحَرَكَاتُ وَخَلَا كُلُّ حَبِيْبٍ بِحَبِيْبِهٖ\nALLAAHUMMA HADA'ATIL ASWAATU WA SAKANATIL HARAKAATU WA KHALAA KULLU HABEEBIN BIHABEEBIH\nO Allah, the voices have quietened, the movements have stilled, and every lover is alone with his beloved;\nوَخَلَوْتُ بِكَ اَنْتَ الْمَحْبُوْبُ اِلَىَّ فَاجْعَلْ خَلْوَتِىْ مِنْكَ اللَّيْلَةَ الْعِتْقَ مِنَ النَّارِ\nWA KHALAWTU BIKA ANTAL MAHBOOBU ILAYYA FAJ'AL KHALWATEE MINKAL LAYLATAL I'TQA MINAN NAAR\nand I am alone with You, for You are the Beloved to me. So make my solitude with You tonight my freedom from the Fire.\nيَا مَنْ لَيْسَتْ لِعَالِمٍ فَوْقَهٗ صِفَةٌ يَا مَنْ لَيْسَ لِمَخْلُوْقٍ دُوْنَهٗ مَنَعَةٌ\nYAA MAN LAYSAT LI-A'ALIMIN FAWQAHOO SIFATUN YAA MAN LAYSA LIMAKHLOOQIN DOONAHOO MANA'AH\nO He above Whom no knower has any attribute! O He without Whom no creature has any protection!\nيَاۤ اَوَّلُ قَبْلَ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ وَيَاۤ اٰخِرًا بَعْدَ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ\nYAA AWWALU QABLA KULLI SHAY'IN WA YAA AAKHIRAN BA'DA KULLI SHAY'\nO First before everything! O Last after everything!\nيَا مَنْ لَيْسَ لَهٗ عُنْصُرٌ وَيَا مَنْ لَيْسَ لِاٰخِرِهٖ فَنَاۤءٌ\nYAA MAN LAYSA LAHOO U'NSURUN WA YAA MAN LAYSA LI-AAKHIRIHEE FANAA'\nO He Who has no element! O He Whose end has no extinction!\nوَيَاۤ اَكْمَلَ مَنْعُوْتٍ وَيَاۤ اَسْمَحَ الْمُعْطِيْنَ وَيَا مَنْ يَفْقَهُ بِكُلِّ لُغَةٍ يُدْعٰى بِهَا\nWA YAA AKMALA MAN'OOTIN WA YAA ASMAHAL MU'TEENA WA YAA MAN YAFQAHU BIKULLI LUGHATIN YUD'AA BIHAA\nO most perfect of all who are described! O most bountiful of all who give! O He Who understands every language in which He is called upon!\nوَيَا مَنْ عَفْوُهٗ قَدِيْمٌ وَبَطْشُهٗ شَدِيْدٌ وَمُلْكُهٗ مُسْتَقِيْمٌ\nWA YAA MAN A'FWUHOO QADEEMUN WA BATSHUHOO SHADEEDUN WA MULKUHOO MUSTAQEEM\nO He Whose pardon is age-old, Whose grip is severe, and Whose kingdom is firmly established!\nاَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ الَّذِىْ شَافَهْتَ بِهٖ مُوْسٰى يَاۤ اَللّٰهُ يَا رَحْمٰنُ يَا رَحِيْمُ يَا لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْتَ\nAS'ALUKA BISMIKAL LADHEE SHAAFAHTA BIHEE MOOSAA YAA ALLAAHU YAA RAHMAANU YAA RAHEEMU YAA LAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANT\nI ask You by Your Name with which You spoke to Musa face to face: O Allah! O Beneficent! O Merciful! O He besides Whom there is no god!\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اَنْتَ الصَّمَدُ اَسْئَلُكَ اَنْ تُصَلِّىَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ وَاَنْ تُدْخِلَنِى الْجَنَّةَ بِرَحْمَتِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA ANTAS SAMADU AS'ALUKA AN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMADIN WA AN TUDKHILANIL JANNATA BIRAHMATIK\nO Allah, You are the Self-Sufficient. I ask You to bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad, and to admit me into Paradise by Your mercy.\nYunus is reported to have asked Imam al-Reza (a.s.) for a brief supplicatory prayer, and the Imam (a.s.) taught him to say:\nيَا مَنْ دَلَّنِىْ عَلٰى نَفْسِهٖ وَذَلَّلَ قَلْبِىْ بِتَصْدِيْقِهٖ اَسْاَلُكَ الْاَمْنَ وَالْاِيْمَانَ\nYAA MAN DALLANEE A'LAA NAFSIHEE WA DHALLALA QALBEE BITASDEEQIHEE AS'ALUKAL AMNA WAL EEMAAN\nO He Who has guided me to Himself and humbled my heart into believing in Him, I ask You for security and faith."
}
